From: starbite <starbite@local>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: 0451-sweet-crash-deep-backtrace.patch - crash backtraces of 40 frames
 (the first 10 on the "CRASH x bt" line as before, the rest on "CRASH x bt+" lines)

Morning test 2026-11-14: tapping the menu bar makes it vanish and come back (Finder dies), System
Settings dies at launch; the 10-frame backtrace stops inside objc_exception_throw. Applies on 0450.
Kernel seq1w = seq1v + this.
---

--- a/osfmk/kern/exception.c	2026-11-14 08:54:10
+++ b/osfmk/kern/exception.c	2026-11-14 08:54:10
@@ -1062,13 +1062,20 @@
 	    get_saved_state_pc(ss), get_saved_state_lr(ss), get_saved_state_sp(ss), fp,
 	    (uint64_t)saved_state64(ss)->far);
 
+	/* 0451: 40 frames (S3z3/the morning test 2026-11-14: Finder and System Settings die on an uncaught exception
+	 * whose 10-frame backtrace stops inside objc_exception_throw); the first 10 on the "bt" line as before,
+	 * the rest on "bt+" lines of 10 */
 	char line[200];
 	int n = snprintf(line, sizeof(line), "CRASH %s bt", name);
-	for (int i = 0; i < 10 && fp != 0 && (fp & 7) == 0 && n < (int)sizeof(line) - 20; i++) {
+	for (int i = 0; i < 40 && fp != 0 && (fp & 7) == 0; i++) {
 		uint64_t frame[2];
 		if (copyin((user_addr_t)fp, frame, sizeof(frame)) != 0) {
 			break;
 		}
+		if (i > 0 && i % 10 == 0) {
+			printf("%s\n", line);
+			n = snprintf(line, sizeof(line), "CRASH %s bt+", name);
+		}
 		n += snprintf(line + n, sizeof(line) - n, " 0x%llx", frame[1]);
 		if (frame[0] <= fp) {
 			break;
